# Supabase STAGING credentials for scripts/supabase_probe.sh and a local app run.
# Copy to .env.staging (gitignored) and fill in. ⚠️ Staging only — never production.
# ⚠️ Use the anon / publishable key. NEVER the service_role key: it bypasses RLS, so every
#    check would pass for the wrong reason.
SUPA_URL=https://your-staging-ref.supabase.co
SUPA_KEY=your-anon-or-publishable-key

# OPTIONAL — the Admin roster only. ⚠️⚠️ This is the **service_role** key and it bypasses RLS completely:
# it can read and write every table regardless of policy. Needed because Stage B revokes `anon`'s access to
# `beta_users`, and the roster's question — "every address" — is one no narrow function can answer.
#
# ⭐ Safe in this file for one reason: Streamlit renders server-side, so it never leaves the machine. That
# reason does NOT transfer — it must never be compiled into a mobile client.
# Project Settings → API → `service_role` `secret` (or Legacy API keys).
SUPA_SERVICE_KEY=
